#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:3
msgid "Tutorial: Parsing text"
msgstr "Tutorial: parsing del testo"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:6
msgid "Database fields"
msgstr "Campi del database"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:7
msgid ""
"phpBB uses the following database fields where BBCode is allowed (forum "
"description, forum rules, post content, ...):"
msgstr ""
"phpBB usa i seguenti campi del database dove è consentito il BBCode "
"(descrizione del forum, regole del forum, contenuto dei messaggi, ...):"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:9
msgid "**foo** - Text itself"
msgstr "**foo** - Il testo stesso"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:10
msgid ""
"**foo_bbcode_uid** - a randomly generated unique identifier to mark the "
"BBCodes and used for quicker parsing"
msgstr ""
"**foo_bbcode_uid** - un identificatore unico generato casualmente per "
"contrassegnare i BBCode, usato per un parsing più rapido"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:11
msgid ""
"**foo_bbcode_bitfield** - a `bit field "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bit_field>`_ containing the information which"
" bbcode is used in the text so only the relevant ones need to be loaded from"
" the database. **NOTE: No longer used in posts generated in phpBB 3.2+**"
msgstr ""
"**foo_bbcode_bitfield** - un `bit field "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bit_field>`_ contenente le informazioni su "
"quali bbcode sono usati nel testo, in modo che solo quelli rilevanti debbano"
" essere caricati dal database. **NOTA: non più usato nei messaggi generati "
"in phpBB 3.2+**"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:12
msgid ""
"**foo_options** - a bit field containing the information whether bbcode, "
"smilies and magic urls are enabled (OPTION_FLAG_BBCODE, OPTION_FLAG_SMILIES "
"and OPTION_FLAG_LINKS). Sometimes you will find this separated into "
"enable_bbcode, enable_smilies and enable_magic_url"
msgstr ""
"**foo_options** - un bit field contenente le informazioni su se bbcode, "
"smilies e magic url sono abilitati (OPTION_FLAG_BBCODE, OPTION_FLAG_SMILIES "
"e OPTION_FLAG_LINKS). A volte lo troverai separato in enable_bbcode, "
"enable_smilies e enable_magic_url"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:14
msgid ""
"Column names will vary, replace ``foo`` with the respective column name "
"(e.g. ``text``, ``text_bbcode_uid``, ...)."
msgstr ""
"I nomi delle colonne variano, sostituisci ``foo`` con il nome della colonna "
"corrispondente (ad es. ``text``, ``text_bbcode_uid``, ...)."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:17
msgid "Parsing text with BBCodes & smilies"
msgstr "Parsing del testo con BBCode e smilies"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:20
msgid "Inserting text into DB"
msgstr "Inserimento del testo nel database"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:39
msgid ""
"The above method uses the bbcode options database field which is used in "
"many places instead of enable_smiles, enable_bbcode and enable_magic_url. "
"Here is how to insert it into the database using the enable_smilies, "
"enable_bbcode and enable_magic_url tables."
msgstr ""
"Il metodo sopra usa il campo del database bbcode options, usato in molti "
"punti al posto di enable_smiles, enable_bbcode e enable_magic_url. Ecco come"
" inserirlo nel database usando le colonne enable_smilies, enable_bbcode e "
"enable_magic_url."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_parsing_text.rst:63
